@* The Notifications module's own imports. Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web is REQUIRED: without it
   @onclick / @bind:event compile as plain HTML attributes, the module builds GREEN and renders, and every click is silently
   dead with no console error. MEASURED 2026-09-15: for an IN-TREE Client module this line is REDUNDANT - the project-root
   src/Stomme.Client/_Imports.razor already carries it and Razor imports cascade, so deleting it here changes nothing
   (NotificationControlClickTests stayed 3/0). It is kept for the day the module leaves the Client project (an external or split
   module has no root import to inherit), which is exactly the BL-54 shape. The click tests pin the defect itself: a plain
   onclick attribute makes bUnit's Click() throw MissingEventHandlerException. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Stomme.Models.Notifications
@using Stomme.Modules.Notifications.Services
@using Stomme.Notifications